The flattened-widget predicate is fixed, and seven families -- not forty -- were publishing its inflated number\n\nTHE FIX. pdf-flattened-widgets.mjs matched `q <cm>... /<anything> Do`. A scanned page\nimage is drawn in exactly that shape, so every scanned page a source ships came back as\nan appearance this build flattened. The pattern now accepts only /FlatWidget-N and\n/ExactFactOverlay-N, the two names the finalizer gives its own output --\nrcap-output-glyph-reading.mjs already restricted itself that way, and two readers of the\nsame bytes were disagreeing.\n\nConfirmed where the defect was found: ar-cs-possession-seal-set's petition fixtures read\n125 before and 41 after, and 41 is the number VF31 established from the bytes three\nindependent ways. Across the family's four fixtures, 308 -> 140.\n\nIt blinds nothing. The eleven families whose placements are ALL images now read 0, which\nis their true count, and not one of those eleven builders imports this module.\n\nAND A CORRECTION TO MY OWN EARLIER REPORT, WHICH I OVERSTATED.\n\nI wrote that 40 families publish an inflated count. What I had measured was what the\nMODULE would report on those families' fixtures. I then carried it as what those\nfamilies publish. So I read every one of the forty families' committed\nreports/actual-writes.json and compared its published total against the module's number\nbefore and after the change, both computed from the committed fixtures:\n\n   7  publish exactly the module's old number -- these the fix corrects, on rebuild\n  11  already publish the module's new number -- never inflated\n  21  publish under this key from some other route, or publish nothing under it at all\n   1  publishes no artifact records whatsoever\n\nENFORCEMENT IS NOT COMPLETE AND I AM NOT CALLING IT COMPLETE. Those seven families'\ncommitted reports still carry the old number. The module is fixed; what they publish is\nnot, and becomes true only when each is rebuilt.\n\nThree separate findings the measurement surfaced, recorded and not repaired:\nfl-self-defense-set publishes 54 appearances where this module reads 0 on both fixtures,\nand it is COMPLETE_PACKET_PROVEN; mo-art-xiv-marijuana-set publishes 2,046 against 598,\nfrom addedGlyphs + vectorMarks under a name that says appearances read from output\nbytes; and ten families publish no value under the key at all on fixtures carrying\nbetween 178 and 886 real finalizer appearances.\n\nTHE ZERO-ARTIFACT-RECORDS CARVE-OUT, MEASURED. PF26 found the completeness verifier\nexempting families with no artifact records from the rule that an unmeasured counter is\nnull. The exemption's stated reason is that \"a zero-source composition binds no document\nbytes by design\". Twenty-one families are exempted by it and every one of them binds\ndocument bytes: nineteen ship fixture PDFs pinned by SHA-256 in their own build-status,\nand the two Ohio families bind their sources by SHA-256 and carry rendered raster pages.\nThe premise is false for its entire population.\n\nTwelve of the twenty-one are counted terminal. That does not make them terminal by a\nfalse zero -- the terminal transition does not read the completeness matrix -- but each\ncarries a PASS_COMPLETE resting on invisibleWrites and visualDefects that nobody\nmeasured. ne-setaside-custodial-set confirms it from the other direction: no artifact\nrecords at all, and 124 real finalizer appearances on its fixtures.\n\nThe verifier is NOT changed here. That change moves what every family publishes and it\nis recorded before it is made, not made on the way past.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T07:40:23Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEa